\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The closed curve in the SNLC column}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{In the SNLC column of \ref{fnip-0086}, take an applied current between
the two folds. The unstable manifold of the saddle meets the stable
node along a short branch and along a long branch, and those branches
form a closed curve. The upper equilibrium stays off that curve. Past
the fold #{\mathrm{SN}_{2}} of Figure 3.6a, the node and the saddle
have disappeared and the curve is a periodic orbit. The upper
equilibrium remains inside it.}

